{"ld": 2149, "paper": "SP867", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Protect Affordability in Mobile Home Parks and Manufactured Housing Communities", "sponsor_id": "s-reny-cameron", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-bailey-donna", "h-golek-cheryl"], "committee_code": "HED", "committee_name": "Housing and Economic Development", "summary": {"text": "This bill does the following.\n\n1. It requires a person renewing a license to operate a manufactured housing community to submit satisfactory evidence to the Manufactured Housing Board.\n\n2. It updates the computation of taxable income of resident individuals and corporations by providing a deduction in an amount equal to any gain recognized on the sale by the taxpayer of an ownership interest greater than 50% in a qualified property if the qualified property was transferred to a cooperative affordable housing corporation, a municipal housing authority or an affiliate of a municipal housing authority.\n\n3. It exempts certain entities that purchase a manufactured housing community or a mobile home park from paying a transfer assessment fee and updates the sworn affirmation of exemption requirement.\n\n4. It establishes liability for damages for a person that is required to pay a transfer assessment fee that fails to do so.\n\n5. It moves from the Department of Professional and Financial Regulation to the Maine State Housing Authority the rule-making authority governing the establishment of a method to determine the net worth of an entity claiming an exemption from certain fees related to the purchase of a mobile home park or a manufactured housing community.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0867&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2026-04-13", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2026-04-13"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text 